"Nathan's antimagic Insight is his own invention, unknown to others and uniquely weighty."
"Nathan's antimagic cost him his own potential to wield magic."
"In the first week, Nathan takes the Antimagic Brawler class, whose blows break barriers."
"Later, Nathan's antimagic breaks wizardry and keeps his memory through Reverse Time."
"Later, Nathan's aura dismantles enemy spellwork and grows to cover a battlefield."
"Later, Nathan blocks detection magic for allies and senses enchantments."
"Later, Nathan breaks slave-collar enchantments without trying."
"Prophecy cannot see Nathan; foresight fails on him, and Davrar cannot predict his outcomes."
"Later, Nathan's aura strips the corruption from blight mana and cleanses blighted land."
"Later, Nathan's aura has a restrained mode letting friendly magic through, and a total denial."
"Later, Nathan's aura spans hundreds of feet, then miles, and stays put while he sleeps."
"Later, Nathan nudges or steadies spells in flight with thin tendrils of antimagic."
"Later, Nathan absorbs others' magical emissions to hide them, and regains Stamina from spells."
"Later, Nathan can block teleports into an area and tease holes through wards unharmed."
"Later, Nathan drains mana pools in seconds and can strip a mage, even a wizard, of magic."
"A mage crippled by antimagic regains magic only through long, arduous effort."
"Later, Nathan's Magical Destruction can break Seals and drain magic from a continent."
"Later, Nathan's antimagic severs wizardry from adamantium, leaving grey dust."
"Later, Nathan bores a pencil-thin hole through Davrar's own arena shell in half a minute."
"Later, Nathan's domain-form aura fuses mana and wizardry to annihilate both."
"Kamus called Nathan's antimagic the archetypal opposite of a Seal."
"Later, Stella and Kamus hold counters to Nathan's antimagic."
"Later, Nathan's Davrar's Denial can deny all skills and Talents, his own included."
"Questors later say Nathan has pushed antimagic farther than anyone on Davrar."
"Nathan's Developments hold that every magic has a counter."
"Later, Aleph Grid Questors demand a ban on antimagic out of fear of Nathan."
